// Implement deepClone(value) that creates a deep copy of the input.
//
// Rules:
// 1. Primitives (number, string, boolean, null, undefined): return as-is
// 2. Date objects: return a new Date with the same time value
// 3. RegExp objects: return a new RegExp with the same pattern and flags
// 4. Arrays: recursively clone each element
// 5. Plain objects: recursively clone each own enumerable property
// 6. Circular references: must be preserved (NOT cause infinite recursion).
//    If object A references object B which references A, the clone must
//    have the same circular structure (cloneA.b.a === cloneA)
// 7. Use a Map to track already-cloned objects for circular reference support
//

